From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: tve: reject modes the CVBS encoder cannot
 produce

rockchip_tve_get_modes() advertises exactly the two entries of cvbs_mode[],
both DRM_MODE_FLAG_INTERLACE. Neither validation hook enforces that:
rockchip_tve_mode_valid() returns MODE_OK for anything, and
rockchip_tve_encoder_atomic_check() never looks at the mode at all.

A client is not restricted to the probed list. A compositor that synthesises
a timing - wlroots does this for a custom resolution - can hand the encoder a
progressive 720x480 and have it accepted. The VOP then programs that timing
verbatim, and on RK3528 the interlace halving disappears from the vertical
side of the crtc state:

  broken:  Display mode: 720x480p59.71   Fixed V: 480 483 493 500
  working: Display mode: 720x480i59.94   Fixed V: 240 240 243 262

CVBS carries no progressive format, so what leaves the DAC is not a signal
any television can lock to.

Add a single predicate for "this is one of the CVBS timings" and use it in
both places, so an unrepresentable mode is dropped from the probed list and
refused at commit rather than being encoded into noise.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_tve.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_tve.c
index f34b6d882..a8327d252 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_tve.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_tve.c
@@ -154,11 +154,32 @@ rockchip_tve_get_modes(struct drm_connector *connector)
 	return count;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The encoder drives CVBS and nothing else: the two entries in cvbs_mode[] are
+ * the only timings it can produce. A client is free to invent a mode and hand
+ * it straight to an atomic commit, so both the probe-time list and the commit
+ * path have to be told that.
+ */
+static bool rockchip_tve_mode_is_cvbs(const struct drm_display_mode *mode)
+{
+	int i;
+
+	if (!(mode->flags & DRM_MODE_FLAG_INTERLACE))
+		return false;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(cvbs_mode); i++)
+		if (mode->hdisplay == cvbs_mode[i].hdisplay &&
+		    mode->vdisplay == cvbs_mode[i].vdisplay)
+			return true;
+
+	return false;
+}
+
 static enum drm_mode_status
 rockchip_tve_mode_valid(struct drm_connector *connector,
 			struct drm_display_mode *mode)
 {
-	return MODE_OK;
+	return rockchip_tve_mode_is_cvbs(mode) ? MODE_OK : MODE_BAD;
 }
 
 static struct drm_encoder *rockchip_tve_best_encoder(struct drm_connector
@@ -556,6 +577,12 @@ rockchip_tve_encoder_atomic_check(struct drm_encoder *encoder,
 	struct drm_connector *connector = conn_state->connector;
 	struct drm_display_info *info = &connector->display_info;
 
+	if (!rockchip_tve_mode_is_cvbs(&crtc_state->adjusted_mode)) {
+		dev_dbg(tve->dev, "%s is not a CVBS mode\n",
+			crtc_state->adjusted_mode.name);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	s->output_mode = ROCKCHIP_OUT_MODE_P888;
 	s->output_type = DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_TV;
 	if (info->num_bus_formats)
